// The left operand of an operator is evaluated once, also when the right one is a
// small integer literal and the left one is a Float or a text.
//
// The VM's compiler tried an immediate form first (`AddIntImm`, `CmpLtImm`, …),
// compiled the left operand, found it a Float, and compiled it again on the general
// path — so `(f() + 0.5) + 1` called `f` twice and printed `f f` (BUG-VMJS-005,
// found by the JavaScript port of the VM). One `f` per line below.

f() {
    >> "f "
    <~ 1.5
}
s() {
    >> "s "
    <~ "t"
}
>> (f() + 0.5) + 1 ¶
>> ((f() + 0.5) < 3) ¶
>> (f() * 2.0) / 3 ¶
>> (f() + 0.5) % 2 ¶
>> f() + 1 ¶
!? {
    x = (s() "a") + 2
} :! {
    >> "error" ¶
}
